{
  "station_schema": 12,
  "name": "FAIRINO FR20 + Gudel TMF-1 Machine Tending",
  "conveyor_simulation_mode": "logical",
  "_comment": [
    "Port of FAIRINO-and-Gudel Machine tending.rdk focused on the FAIRINO FR20 and Gudel TMF-1 6 m.",
    "The source side uses a PhysX spawner capped at 10 active products feeding a four-corner parametric pick accumulator banked toward the robot.",
    "The FAIRINO carries the built-in Robotiq Hand-E Dual Gripper. The redesigned pick feeder uses a sub-two-box-width single-file intake, a compact centre platform, deck-following side walls and a full-height terminal wall. Machine Tending Demo selects the left TCP for its logical pick and the right TCP for its PhysX pick, services the same repeatable end-stop nest from directly above on elbow-up analytic IK branches, carries both boxes to the far end, deposits both onto the output conveyor, and returns to a safe pose before looping.",
    "The robot and TMF-1 share the station-only fr20-tmf1 motion link. Program MoveJ/MoveL lines may append J7 in millimetres; the demo carries both boxes to J7=6400 and unloads them onto the PhysX output conveyor before looping.",
    "The rail starts at external-axis position 0.",
    "Robot and conveyor placements are mapped from RoboDK Z-up to RobotSimulator Y-up coordinates, then translated so the rail is centered around the station origin."
  ],
